File: src/notifications/templates.ts
The issue #4201 highlights that the password reset email contains a link pointing to `http://localhost:3000`, which is obviously incorrect for deployed environments. Upon inspecting `src/notifications/templates.ts`, the problem is due to the `BASE_URL` constant being set as `process.env.PUBLIC_URL ?? "http://localhost:3000"`. This fallback to localhost is causing the email links to be wrong when the environment variable `PUBLIC_URL` is not set.

The proposed fix is to make sure that the environment variable `PUBLIC_URL` is set appropriately in the production environment configuration, or to modify the code to use a more robust method for determining the public URL. However, since this PR is only a draft proposal describing the issue and location, the main change is to note the affected code for further fix.

File: `src/notifications/templates.ts`
Context:
```typescript
const BASE_URL = process.env.PUBLIC_URL ?? "http://localhost:3000";

export function passwordResetEmail(user: Recipient, token: string): EmailMessage {
  const link = `${BASE_URL}/reset-password?token=${token}`;
  return {
    to: user.email,
    subject: t("email.reset.subject", {}, user.locale),
    text: t(
      "email.reset.body",
      { name: user.name, link, minutes: config.auth.resetTokenTtlMinutes },
      user.locale,
    ),
  };
}
```

This needs to be corrected so that the reset-password links in emails use the correct URL in all environments.

